(1377635, 176138, 19010, '<td valign="top">I think I would have cropped this right above the blue.</td>', 'I think I would have cropped this right above the blue.', '2005-05-11 09:03:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377636, 176055, 19961, '<td valign="top">Could have benefitted from more contrast I thought.</td>', 'Could have benefitted from more contrast I thought.', '2005-05-11 09:03:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377645, 175209, 36722, '<td valign="top">with this kind of minimal photography, you need to either get the whole object into your frame, or make a clear choice to cut off a part. not cut off such a tiny little corner.<br/>otherwise excellent photo, OK for the challenge.</td>', 'with this kind of minimal photography, you need to either get the whole object into your frame, or make a clear choice to cut off a part. not cut off such a tiny little corner.otherwise excellent photo, OK for the challenge.', '2005-05-11 09:08:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377646, 176219, 36722, '<td valign="top">i think you''ve overdone the DoF a bit here.</td>', 'i think you''ve overdone the DoF a bit here.', '2005-05-11 09:09:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377650, 176480, 34591, '<td valign="top">I think this would have been much nicer without the cigarette pack in the shot. Nice job though.</td>', 'I think this would have been much nicer without the cigarette pack in the shot. Nice job though.', '2005-05-11 09:11:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377651, 176730, 34247, '<td valign="top">Composition is nice, but sharper focus on the face and softer light fall on the right side of this image would have resulted in a more effective image.</td>', 'Composition is nice, but sharper focus on the face and softer light fall on the right side of this image would have resulted in a more effective image.', '2005-05-11 09:13:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377653, 175486, 34247, '<td valign="top">I like the composition a lot, with the foreground triangles evocative of something older and well used. The dodge job is a bit too much, I feel, and the background, with cars on the right side presenting several points of distraction. Deeper bokeh would have worked well here, imho.</td>', 'I like the composition a lot, with the foreground triangles evocative of something older and well used. The dodge job is a bit too much, I feel, and the background, with cars on the right side presenting several points of distraction. Deeper bokeh would have worked well here, imho.', '2005-05-11 09:15:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377655, 175127, 34247, '<td valign="top">Nice perspective. For this to be more effective, however, there should be more detailing present in the triangular shapes, and the background of blue sky doesn''t contribute much. Maybe if the color tones were played with a little bit, creating greater contrast perhaps, then it would be a more effective image for me.</td>', 'Nice perspective. For this to be more effective, however, there should be more detailing present in the triangular shapes, and the background of blue sky doesn''t contribute much. Maybe if the color tones were played with a little bit, creating greater contrast perhaps, then it would be a more effective image for me.', '2005-05-11 09:17:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377656, 176377, 33982, '<td valign="top">horizon horizon horizon</td>', 'horizon horizon horizon', '2005-05-11 09:17:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377658, 175189, 32595, '<td valign="top">seems your triangle is the only thing out of focuse</td>', 'seems your triangle is the only thing out of focuse', '2005-05-11 09:18:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377659, 176486, 34247, '<td valign="top">One of the first wow pictures of this challenge-vote round for me, and it''s very striking. I like the shifting color tones a lot, and the reddish tint on the right side is very evocative in terms of mood. I can''t help but think that this would also have scored well with me in the upcoming silhouette challenge. If there were complaints to be made, I''d say the tuft of cloud and little flare on the upper left, and the reflection on the water surface, which could have been burned in some more. But alas, it''s basic edit, and given the parameters, I''ll still score this my first 10 of the challenge. Thanks.</td>', 'One of the first wow pictures of this challenge-vote round for me, and it''s very striking. I like the shifting color tones a lot, and the reddish tint on the right side is very evocative in terms of mood. I can''t help but think that this would also have scored well with me in the upcoming silhouette challenge. If there were complaints to be made, I''d say the tuft of cloud and little flare on the upper left, and the reflection on the water surface, which could have been burned in some more. But alas, it''s basic edit, and given the parameters, I''ll still score this my first 10 of the challenge. Thanks.', '2005-05-11 09:20:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377662, 174214, 34247, '<td valign="top">I think there''s too much distraction points in this image as it is now. A closer crop on the triangular shape would have yielded an effective picture both within and out of the context of the challenge.</td>', 'I think there''s too much distraction points in this image as it is now. A closer crop on the triangular shape would have yielded an effective picture both within and out of the context of the challenge.', '2005-05-11 09:21:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377663, 174215, 32595, '<td valign="top">a little more DOF i think would have helped</td>', 'a little more DOF i think would have helped', '2005-05-11 09:22:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377664, 175257, 32595, '<td valign="top">pic seems soft nice color</td>', 'pic seems soft nice color', '2005-05-11 09:22:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377666, 175386, 34247, '<td valign="top">The lighting feels too harsh and the presentation in a colorful plate doesn''t work as well for me. I think a softer light, clearer focus on the roti, and a "calmer" more subdued background would have been more effective here.</td>', 'The lighting feels too harsh and the presentation in a colorful plate doesn''t work as well for me. I think a softer light, clearer focus on the roti, and a "calmer" more subdued background would have been more effective here.', '2005-05-11 09:23:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377668, 174756, 13610, '<td valign="top">The image is tilted. The idea is good and we photographer should have thought of it first time. (I personnally have my tripod in front of me on my desk all the tiem and never saw a damn triangle on this thing!) If you were ever to reshoot this, I''d suggest that you fill a whole 3rd of your image with the triangle part of the tripod in close-up and fill the rest with a blurry background, and no flash.</td>', 'The image is tilted. The idea is good and we photographer should have thought of it first time. (I personnally have my tripod in front of me on my desk all the tiem and never saw a damn triangle on this thing!) If you were ever to reshoot this, I''d suggest that you fill a whole 3rd of your image with the triangle part of the tripod in close-up and fill the rest with a blurry background, and no flash.', '2005-05-11 09:24:38.000000', NULL, 1),
