(1381633, 176541, 19780, '<td valign="top">Great shot - very imaginative and simple. I like the choice of b&amp;w and going high-key. However, the white inset border kind of messes with the composition on the right side - maybe a hairline black and then the white and again the black would have worked better? It''s really a minor complaint on a wonderful shot.  8</td>', 'Great shot - very imaginative and simple. I like the choice of b&w and going high-key. However, the white inset border kind of messes with the composition on the right side - maybe a hairline black and then the white and again the black would have worked better? It''s really a minor complaint on a wonderful shot.  8', '2005-05-12 15:58:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1381639, 175271, 7743, '<td valign="top">I see two different compositions in this image.  One using the symmetry of the railing and its reflection and the other with the railing, tree and bench.  <br/> <br/>For the latter, cropping most of the reflection and not cropping as much on top would make a very tranquil image.  To exploit the symmetry a vertical composition might work better and I don''t think the tree and bench are needed.<br/> <br/>In either case, more contrast would probably increase the impact of the image. 6</td>', 'I see two different compositions in this image.  One using the symmetry of the railing and its reflection and the other with the railing, tree and bench.   For the latter, cropping most of the reflection and not cropping as much on top would make a very tranquil image.  To exploit the symmetry a vertical composition might work better and I don''t think the tree and bench are needed. In either case, more contrast would probably increase the impact of the image. 6', '2005-05-12 16:02:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1381641, 175700, 19010, '<td valign="top">A little to sft. I also feel that this would have worked better if it had not been shot from a directly over head angle. I will admit though I just noticed the water? in the background now thats a little different and worthy of bumbing this one up a point.</td>', 'A little to sft. I also feel that this would have worked better if it had not been shot from a directly over head angle. I will admit though I just noticed the water? in the background now thats a little different and worthy of bumbing this one up a point.', '2005-05-12 16:03:09.000000', NULL, 1),
