(1395684, 176383, 20056, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments, few but what could I expect with this picture :)?<br/> <br/>Those who did not read the book, maybe did not get much of the meaning... the book talks about symbols and how religions use those symbols in their interest... behind symbols there are ideas: So, the picture shows Christian''s crux breaking the David''s star because Catholic church was interested in a  male God rather than a female/male dual God represented by David''s star ("it shows a balance between masculinity and femininity, the upward pointing triangle being symbolic of man and the downward pointing triangle being symbolic of woman.")<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-05-18 16:19:26.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the comments, few but what could I expect with this picture :)? Those who did not read the book, maybe did not get much of the meaning... the book talks about symbols and how religions use those symbols in their interest... behind symbols there are ideas: So, the picture shows Christian''s crux breaking the David''s star because Catholic church was interested in a  male God rather than a female/male dual God represented by David''s star ("it shows a balance between masculinity and femininity, the upward pointing triangle being symbolic of man and the downward pointing triangle being symbolic of woman.")', '2005-05-18 17:08:47.000000', '2005-05-18 17:19:26.000000', 0),
(1395691, 176383, 20056, '<td valign="top"><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-05-18 16:12:33.</i></td>', '', '2005-05-18 17:11:39.000000', '2005-05-18 17:12:33.000000', 0),
(1395721, 175328, 34396, '<td valign="top">This is really an awesome photo.  I think it was misjudged in the voting by many.  The two triangles that make up this photo are so "in your face" that you blow right past them looking for something less obvious.  I know that I missed it during voting.  The triangle I found was the one formed by the water.  "Yeah, OK, its a triangle"...I read the title "False Convergence" and started looking deeper into the center of the photo for a triangle.  "OK, I vaguely see another where the points come together in the center."  It is not until now that I see the brilliance of this photo.  The two halves of the photo forming distinctly different contrasts and colors.  I am truly sorry that I missed it in voting or you would have gotten a much better score from me.  I think art sometimes requires time for it to "soak in".  Even as I go back to look at it while writing this I am seeing more.  The building top at the upper left forming another contrasting triangle.  Superb work!</td>', 'This is really an awesome photo.  I think it was misjudged in the voting by many.  The two triangles that make up this photo are so "in your face" that you blow right past them looking for something less obvious.  I know that I missed it during voting.  The triangle I found was the one formed by the water.  "Yeah, OK, its a triangle"...I read the title "False Convergence" and started looking deeper into the center of the photo for a triangle.  "OK, I vaguely see another where the points come together in the center."  It is not until now that I see the brilliance of this photo.  The two halves of the photo forming distinctly different contrasts and colors.  I am truly sorry that I missed it in voting or you would have gotten a much better score from me.  I think art sometimes requires time for it to "soak in".  Even as I go back to look at it while writing this I am seeing more.  The building top at the upper left forming another contrasting triangle.  Superb work!', '2005-05-18 17:19:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1395723, 176023, 13736, '<td valign="top">Thanx to Everybody for to comments and votes!<br/>:)<br/>So I shoot this picture at a fire-show in my town''s castle. This was the very first moment. I put my camera to the tripod, and shoot a trial, and in this moment the girl lighted the fire, so I coludn''t change the expo time. (10 sec) Thats why a little bit over burned. In PS I had played by the saturation and the hue. Thats all. Good lights to all of You!</td>', 'Thanx to Everybody for to comments and votes!:)So I shoot this picture at a fire-show in my town''s castle. This was the very first moment. I put my camera to the tripod, and shoot a trial, and in this moment the girl lighted the fire, so I coludn''t change the expo time. (10 sec) Thats why a little bit over burned. In PS I had played by the saturation and the hue. Thats all. Good lights to all of You!', '2005-05-18 17:19:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1395828, 175294, 25655, '<td valign="top">Didn''t vote on it during the challenge (I know... I know it''s not nice of me! but I was already reprimended ;-) but thinking of it right now, I guess I would have given it a 6 or a 7.<br/>Several things that I love here:<br/>first - the set-up. The stage is wonderful, the lights are awsome, the composition is a little bit busy but has a very dynamic feel.<br/>In addition - I just love cellos and contrabasses, and would vote high on them any time. <br/>I recognized the 3 microphones right away, got your triangle and loved that out-side of the box thinking.<br/>I also like that alerted anticipation in the photo, as if the instruments are going to start playing any second now, with or without their players.<br/> <br/>What lowers this photo''s score in the challenge is only the lack in "triangle shape" as the challenge stated.<br/>Other then that this one is a pure beauty!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Didn''t vote on it during the challenge (I know... I know it''s not nice of me! but I was already reprimended ;-) but thinking of it right now, I guess I would have given it a 6 or a 7.Several things that I love here:first - the set-up. The stage is wonderful, the lights are awsome, the composition is a little bit busy but has a very dynamic feel.In addition - I just love cellos and contrabasses, and would vote high on them any time. I recognized the 3 microphones right away, got your triangle and loved that out-side of the box thinking.I also like that alerted anticipation in the photo, as if the instruments are going to start playing any second now, with or without their players. What lowers this photo''s score in the challenge is only the lack in "triangle shape" as the challenge stated.Other then that this one is a pure beauty! ', '2005-05-18 17:46:07.000000', NULL, 0),
