(1401044, 176512, 14614, '<td valign="top">didn''t get to voting on 100% in this challenge and missed this one.  Quite a lot to like here.  Sepia keeps my eye on the composition and the forms.  You''ve captured several strong, simple geometric shapes that work well against each other.  The shimmer in the water adds movement to the image and keeps the shapes from being too "heavy"   The duck adds life and whimsy ... as does the facing "duck shape" in the metal object.  Great balance of many complex elements!</td>', 'didn''t get to voting on 100% in this challenge and missed this one.  Quite a lot to like here.  Sepia keeps my eye on the composition and the forms.  You''ve captured several strong, simple geometric shapes that work well against each other.  The shimmer in the water adds movement to the image and keeps the shapes from being too "heavy"   The duck adds life and whimsy ... as does the facing "duck shape" in the metal object.  Great balance of many complex elements!', '2005-05-20 16:17:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(1401541, 176512, 26464, '<td valign="top">great tones, texture, title, challenge relevance, the whole deal. this should be top 10. pity i didn''t see this while voting to help bump it up. <br/></td>', 'great tones, texture, title, challenge relevance, the whole deal. this should be top 10. pity i didn''t see this while voting to help bump it up. ', '2005-05-20 21:11:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(1401725, 174322, 37380, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the great feedback everyone!<br/> <br/>Well, I''m pretty chuffed with how well my first entry did, especially considering the fact that I only bothered taking two photos (The first was out of focus, and once I took the second one I immediately liked it). My only regret is not having spent more time processing the raw image to see if I could avoid the blown-out areas of the image. Oh well, live and learn. Perhaps I''ll spot-edit it if I ever make a print to hang on the wall.<br/> <br/>-cB<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks for the great feedback everyone! Well, I''m pretty chuffed with how well my first entry did, especially considering the fact that I only bothered taking two photos (The first was out of focus, and once I took the second one I immediately liked it). My only regret is not having spent more time processing the raw image to see if I could avoid the blown-out areas of the image. Oh well, live and learn. Perhaps I''ll spot-edit it if I ever make a print to hang on the wall. -cB ', '2005-05-20 22:54:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(1401763, 176512, 27812, '<td valign="top">I have given this pic a 10, it is a masterpiece. Vibrant in every respect. You remain a master my friend!</td>', 'I have given this pic a 10, it is a masterpiece. Vibrant in every respect. You remain a master my friend!', '2005-05-20 23:18:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1402000, 175693, 36299, '<td valign="top">I scored this a ten.  Only one I see.  Here is my reason why:  First, I am not an American.  Despise quite a bit about what their government does.  My initial reaction to such things is 1.  Political statements are so very boring.  Even if it is Chilean rebelling against Pinochet in those days.  I was at a friends house who received a phone call that his past lover in Chile was bayoneted in the stomach a few hours earlier and had died.  He was distraught, it was a long night, but out of that night came a very interesting conversation.<br/> <br/>The family had worked on the family, and had not spent a dime on its comforts.  The wall in this image is of, in my mind, the cheap fake wood panel you put up, no less then other families, not because you cannot buy better, but because that money can be better used for the family.  For all this family has done, they have a flag, in a triangle on a wall.  Courtesy of an ideal.  My children will never suffer this.  Although they maybe the cause.</td>', 'I scored this a ten.  Only one I see.  Here is my reason why:  First, I am not an American.  Despise quite a bit about what their government does.  My initial reaction to such things is 1.  Political statements are so very boring.  Even if it is Chilean rebelling against Pinochet in those days.  I was at a friends house who received a phone call that his past lover in Chile was bayoneted in the stomach a few hours earlier and had died.  He was distraught, it was a long night, but out of that night came a very interesting conversation. The family had worked on the family, and had not spent a dime on its comforts.  The wall in this image is of, in my mind, the cheap fake wood panel you put up, no less then other families, not because you cannot buy better, but because that money can be better used for the family.  For all this family has done, they have a flag, in a triangle on a wall.  Courtesy of an ideal.  My children will never suffer this.  Although they maybe the cause.', '2005-05-21 02:49:20.000000', NULL, 0),
