(1411473, 176457, 19746, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by flip89:</b></div><hr/><i> Not sure what happened here, Alex.  Very original and well thought of.   I thought this would be up there in the top twenty at least.  But 85 percentile is not bad. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks man, I was a little disappointed too.  I was quite happy with my idea and it got me to take this photo, which I like :) I appreciate your comment!<br/> <br/>Alex</td>', 'Originally posted by flip89: Not sure what happened here, Alex.  Very original and well thought of.   I thought this would be up there in the top twenty at least.  But 85 percentile is not bad.   Thanks man, I was a little disappointed too.  I was quite happy with my idea and it got me to take this photo, which I like :) I appreciate your comment! Alex', '2005-05-25 12:44:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1413753, 176740, 27886, '<td valign="top"><b>The problem with the wires is that they aren''t gray/silver/black, they are actually glow in the dark green. So making them dark without loosing the sky too, was hard without going beyond any advanced editing rules. I just upped the contrast and desaturated.</b></td>', 'The problem with the wires is that they aren''t gray/silver/black, they are actually glow in the dark green. So making them dark without loosing the sky too, was hard without going beyond any advanced editing rules. I just upped the contrast and desaturated.', '2005-05-26 13:00:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(1415430, 175486, 19746, '<td valign="top">I was right!  Those Telkom phone booths are spottable a mile away!  I think you captured this about as well as you possibly could have given the situation, you couldn''t risk too shallow a DOF and I presume it wouldn''t have worked from the other side?  Love the textures.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I was right!  Those Telkom phone booths are spottable a mile away!  I think you captured this about as well as you possibly could have given the situation, you couldn''t risk too shallow a DOF and I presume it wouldn''t have worked from the other side?  Love the textures. ', '2005-05-27 07:34:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1418929, 175885, 17126, '<td valign="top">Sweet. This picture is really awesome. Thanks for telling us how you framed it. I think a lot of pictures would benefit from a frame like that - it creates a vintage feel, don''t you think?</td>', 'Sweet. This picture is really awesome. Thanks for telling us how you framed it. I think a lot of pictures would benefit from a frame like that - it creates a vintage feel, don''t you think?', '2005-05-29 14:13:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1423606, 176225, 3087, '<td valign="top">Centred composition works well. I like the way the object seems to be floating. Lighting is generally OK - too strong would mean losing the nice detail on the metal work moulding - but it''s not very even. The lower left area of the frame seems darker than the rest. Perhaps a light reflector might help with that? In terms of content, it''s not an exciting shot, though it certainly meets the challenge and is well executed. My main reaction is, nicely done shot of a quirky object, move on. I need something more to hook my attention.</td>', 'Centred composition works well. I like the way the object seems to be floating. Lighting is generally OK - too strong would mean losing the nice detail on the metal work moulding - but it''s not very even. The lower left area of the frame seems darker than the rest. Perhaps a light reflector might help with that? In terms of content, it''s not an exciting shot, though it certainly meets the challenge and is well executed. My main reaction is, nicely done shot of a quirky object, move on. I need something more to hook my attention.', '2005-05-31 16:40:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1425194, 176567, 12619, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by graphicfunk:</b></div><hr/><i> Now, this is a nice composition and very inventive at that. This image could have excelled with the focus on top of the hands and then a white balance correction. Another simpler solution is to desaturate the image a bit so as to remove the reddish overcast. 6 </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks, your photos are very good.<br/>I did this in 20 minutes..teaches me to be tardy next time..<br/>Thanks also for the tips - from the world of film, just getting comfortable with editing.</td>', 'Originally posted by graphicfunk: Now, this is a nice composition and very inventive at that. This image could have excelled with the focus on top of the hands and then a white balance correction. Another simpler solution is to desaturate the image a bit so as to remove the reddish overcast. 6  Thanks, your photos are very good.I did this in 20 minutes..teaches me to be tardy next time..Thanks also for the tips - from the world of film, just getting comfortable with editing.', '2005-06-01 03:33:28.000000', NULL, 0),
